Read and fully absorbed. All clarifications are clear. Let me give you the final consolidated plan before we touch a single file.

FACET CRM — Final Architecture & Migration Plan

FINAL ARCHITECTURE SUMMARY

COMPANY (root entity)
  ├── CONTACTS (belong to company, multiple allowed)
  ├── PROJECTS (belong to company, multiple allowed)
  │     ├── ACTIVITIES (rep's daily interactions, linked to project + company)
  │     └── QUOTATIONS (coordinator-entered, linked to project + company + rep)
  └── COMPANY_REPS (junction: which reps own/share this company)

Roles (4 total):

rep — own companies/contacts/projects/activities. Never sees other reps' activities.

manager — full visibility + approval authority over everything.

sales_coordinator — quotation coordination layer. Sees all quotations. Does NOT see rep activity details.

marketing — basically a rep + can register leads. Manager assigns or keeps with marketing user.

Key Rules locked in:

Only manager can delete companies, contacts, projects.

Reps cannot delete — only edit their own records.

Shared company = both reps see the company entity, but each sees ONLY their own activities.

Free-text company entry in daily report → removed. Dropdown only going forward.

All notifications → in-app only. No WhatsApp/email for now.

Friday + Saturday = off days in any scheduling logic.

FINAL DB MIGRATION ORDER

Here is the safest sequence — each step is safe to run independently.

STEP 1 — Fix Role Constraint (reps table)

Adds sales_coordinator and marketing to allowed roles.

alter table reps drop constraint if exists reps_role_check;
alter table reps add constraint reps_role_check
  check (role in ('rep','manager','sales_coordinator','marketing'));

STEP 2 — Fix Company Type Constraint (companies/customers table)

This is the canonical final list. Run this to sync DB with business reality.

alter table customers drop constraint if exists customers_company_type_check;
alter table customers add constraint customers_company_type_check
  check (company_type in (
    'Factory','Advertising','Real Estate','Owner','Consultant',
    'Contractor','Station Management','Workshop','Other'
  ));

⚠️ Note: I corrected "Real State" → "Real Estate" and "Station Managment" → "Station Management". Update your UI dropdowns to match exactly.

STEP 3 — Rename customers → companies (carefully)

alter table customers rename to companies;
alter table duplicate_flags rename column customer_id_1 to company_id_1;
alter table duplicate_flags rename column customer_id_2 to company_id_2;

STEP 4 — Add branches table

create table if not exists branches (
  id         uuid primary key default uuid_generate_v4(),
  name       text not null,
  region     text not null check (region in ('Central','West','East','North','South')),
  is_active  boolean default true,
  created_at timestamptz default now()
);

-- Seed current 3 branches
insert into branches (name, region) values
  ('Riyadh', 'Central'),
  ('Eastern Branch', 'East'),
  ('Southern Branch', 'South');

STEP 5 — Add branch_id to reps + language_pref

alter table reps add column if not exists branch_id uuid references branches(id);
alter table reps add column if not exists language_pref text default 'en' 
  check (language_pref in ('en','ar'));

STEP 6 — Add branch_id to companies

alter table companies add column if not exists branch_id uuid references branches(id);

STEP 7 — Drop shared_with from companies (after junction table is created)

First create the junction table, THEN drop the old column.

create table if not exists company_reps (
  id          uuid primary key default uuid_generate_v4(),
  company_id  uuid not null references companies(id) on delete cascade,
  rep_id      uuid not null references reps(id) on delete cascade,
  role        text not null default 'primary' 
              check (role in ('primary','shared')),
  assigned_by uuid references reps(id),
  assigned_at timestamptz default now(),
  unique(company_id, rep_id)
);

-- Migrate existing primary_rep_id data into junction table
insert into company_reps (company_id, rep_id, role)
select id, primary_rep_id, 'primary'
from companies
where primary_rep_id is not null
on conflict do nothing;

-- Now safe to drop old column
alter table companies drop column if exists shared_with;
-- Keep primary_rep_id for now as a quick-lookup cache (optional but useful)
-- We'll decide later whether to fully drop it

STEP 8 — Create contacts table

create sequence if not exists contact_code_seq start 1;

create table if not exists contacts (
  id             uuid primary key default uuid_generate_v4(),
  contact_code   text unique,
  company_id     uuid not null references companies(id) on delete cascade,
  full_name      text not null,
  full_name_ar   text,
  title          text,
  phone          text,
  whatsapp       text,
  email          text,
  is_primary     boolean default false,
  notes          text,
  created_by     uuid references reps(id),
  created_at     timestamptz default now(),
  updated_at     timestamptz default now()
);

create or replace function set_contact_code()
returns trigger language plpgsql as $$
begin
  if new.contact_code is null then
    new.contact_code := 'CON-' || lpad(nextval('contact_code_seq')::text, 5, '0');
  end if;
  return new;
end;
$$;

create trigger trg_contact_code before insert on contacts
  for each row execute function set_contact_code();

create trigger trg_contacts_updated before update on contacts
  for each row execute function set_updated_at();

STEP 9 — Update projects table

-- Add new fields
alter table projects add column if not exists contact_id uuid references contacts(id);
alter table projects add column if not exists stage_changed_at timestamptz default now();
alter table projects add column if not exists next_follow_up date;
alter table projects add column if not exists loss_reason text;

-- Create project_reps junction table
create table if not exists project_reps (
  id          uuid primary key default uuid_generate_v4(),
  project_id  uuid not null references projects(id) on delete cascade,
  rep_id      uuid not null references reps(id) on delete cascade,
  role        text not null default 'primary'
              check (role in ('primary','shared')),
  sqm_split   numeric,
  assigned_by uuid references reps(id),
  assigned_at timestamptz default now(),
  unique(project_id, rep_id)
);

-- Migrate existing assigned_rep_id data
insert into project_reps (project_id, rep_id, role)
select id, assigned_rep_id, 'primary'
from projects
where assigned_rep_id is not null
on conflict do nothing;

-- Drop old columns (after verifying migration above worked)
alter table projects drop column if exists shared_with;
alter table projects drop column if exists sqm_split;
-- Keep assigned_rep_id as cache for now (same as companies)

STEP 10 — Update activities table

alter table activities add column if not exists company_id uuid references companies(id);
alter table activities add column if not exists project_id uuid references projects(id);
alter table activities add column if not exists contact_id uuid references contacts(id);
-- rep_name kept for legacy display, but queries should join reps table going forward

STEP 11 — Create quotations table

create sequence if not exists quotation_code_seq start 1;

create table if not exists quotations (
  id               uuid primary key default uuid_generate_v4(),
  quotation_code   text unique,
  project_id       uuid not null references projects(id) on delete cascade,
  company_id       uuid not null references companies(id),
  rep_id           uuid references reps(id),
  coordinator_id   uuid references reps(id),
  product_type     text check (product_type in (
                     'Normal ACP','FR B1 ACP','FR A2 ACP','A2G2 ACP','Other'
                   )),
  finish           text check (finish in ('Solid Color','Wood Finish','Custom')),
  sqm_quoted       numeric not null default 0,
  price_per_sqm    numeric,
  quote_date       date not null default current_date,
  valid_until      date,
  revision_number  integer default 1,
  status           text default 'pending' check (status in (
                     'pending','submitted','won','lost','expired','cancelled'
                   )),
  sqm_invoiced     numeric default 0,
  sqm_delivered    numeric default 0,
  notes            text,
  created_at       timestamptz default now(),
  updated_at       timestamptz default now()
);

create or replace function set_quotation_code()
returns trigger language plpgsql as $$
begin
  if new.quotation_code is null then
    new.quotation_code := 'QUO-' || lpad(nextval('quotation_code_seq')::text, 5, '0');
  end if;
  return new;
end;
$$;

create trigger trg_quotation_code before insert on quotations
  for each row execute function set_quotation_code();

create trigger trg_quotations_updated before update on quotations
  for each row execute function set_updated_at();

STEP 12 — Create notifications table

create table if not exists notifications (
  id           uuid primary key default uuid_generate_v4(),
  recipient_id uuid not null references reps(id) on delete cascade,
  type         text not null check (type in (
                 'duplicate_alert','pending_approval','assignment',
                 'project_stale','quotation_expiry','follow_up_due',
                 'lead_submitted','system'
               )),
  title        text not null,
  body         text,
  entity_type  text check (entity_type in ('company','contact','project','quotation','rep')),
  entity_id    uuid,
  is_read      boolean default false,
  created_at   timestamptz default now()
);

STEP 13 — Add all indexes

create index if not exists idx_activities_rep_id on activities(rep_id);
create index if not exists idx_activities_date on activities(activity_date);
create index if not exists idx_activities_company_id on activities(company_id);
create index if not exists idx_activities_project_id on activities(project_id);
create index if not exists idx_company_reps_company on company_reps(company_id);
create index if not exists idx_company_reps_rep on company_reps(rep_id);
create index if not exists idx_project_reps_project on project_reps(project_id);
create index if not exists idx_project_reps_rep on project_reps(rep_id);
create index if not exists idx_contacts_company on contacts(company_id);
create index if not exists idx_projects_company on projects(customer_id);
create index if not exists idx_projects_stage on projects(stage);
create index if not exists idx_quotations_project on quotations(project_id);
create index if not exists idx_quotations_rep on quotations(rep_id);
create index if not exists idx_notifications_recipient on notifications(recipient_id, is_read);
create index if not exists idx_reps_auth_user on reps(auth_user_id);

STEP 14 — Update RLS policies

-- Helper: expand role check
-- (existing current_user_role() function already works, no change needed)

-- Companies: manager full, rep via junction, marketing insert only
drop policy if exists "customers_manager" on companies;
create policy "companies_manager" on companies for all
  using (current_user_role() = 'manager');

drop policy if exists "customers_rep_read" on companies;
create policy "companies_rep_read" on companies for select
  using (
    current_user_role() in ('rep','marketing') and
    exists (
      select 1 from company_reps
      where company_reps.company_id = companies.id
      and company_reps.rep_id = current_rep_id()
    )
  );

drop policy if exists "customers_rep_update" on companies;
create policy "companies_rep_update" on companies for update
  using (
    current_user_role() = 'rep' and
    exists (
      select 1 from company_reps
      where company_reps.company_id = companies.id
      and company_reps.rep_id = current_rep_id()
    )
  );

create policy "companies_rep_insert" on companies for insert
  with check (current_user_role() in ('rep','marketing','manager'));

-- Coordinator read on companies and projects
create policy "companies_coordinator_read" on companies for select
  using (current_user_role() = 'sales_coordinator');

-- Contacts: follow company access
alter table contacts enable row level security;
create policy "contacts_manager" on contacts for all
  using (current_user_role() = 'manager');
create policy "contacts_rep_access" on contacts for select
  using (
    current_user_role() in ('rep','marketing') and
    exists (
      select 1 from company_reps
      where company_reps.company_id = contacts.company_id
      and company_reps.rep_id = current_rep_id()
    )
  );
create policy "contacts_rep_insert" on contacts for insert
  with check (current_user_role() in ('rep','marketing'));
create policy "contacts_rep_update" on contacts for update
  using (
    current_user_role() = 'rep' and
    exists (
      select 1 from company_reps
      where company_reps.company_id = contacts.company_id
      and company_reps.rep_id = current_rep_id()
    )
  );

-- Projects: rep via junction
alter table projects enable row level security;
drop policy if exists "projects_manager" on projects;
create policy "projects_manager" on projects for all
  using (current_user_role() = 'manager');

drop policy if exists "projects_rep_read" on projects;
create policy "projects_rep_read" on projects for select
  using (
    current_user_role() in ('rep','marketing') and
    exists (
      select 1 from project_reps
      where project_reps.project_id = projects.id
      and project_reps.rep_id = current_rep_id()
    )
  );
create policy "projects_rep_insert" on projects for insert
  with check (current_user_role() in ('rep','marketing','manager'));
create policy "projects_rep_update" on projects for update
  using (
    current_user_role() in ('rep','marketing') and
    exists (
      select 1 from project_reps
      where project_reps.project_id = projects.id
      and project_reps.rep_id = current_rep_id()
    )
  );
create policy "projects_coordinator_read" on projects for select
  using (current_user_role() = 'sales_coordinator');

-- Quotations
alter table quotations enable row level security;
create policy "quotations_manager_coordinator" on quotations for all
  using (current_user_role() in ('manager','sales_coordinator'));
create policy "quotations_rep_read" on quotations for select
  using (current_user_role() in ('rep','marketing') and rep_id = current_rep_id());

-- Notifications: each user sees only their own
alter table notifications enable row level security;
create policy "notifications_own" on notifications for all
  using (recipient_id = current_rep_id());

-- company_reps and project_reps: manager full, others read-only
alter table company_reps enable row level security;
create policy "company_reps_manager" on company_reps for all
  using (current_user_role() = 'manager');
create policy "company_reps_rep_read" on company_reps for select
  using (rep_id = current_rep_id());

alter table project_reps enable row level security;
create policy "project_reps_manager" on project_reps for all
  using (current_user_role() = 'manager');
create policy "project_reps_rep_read" on project_reps for select
  using (rep_id = current_rep_id());

